    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #317\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch `bb/relay-212-implementation-audit-fixes-02-23-add-r-thr_wes8xwzz2f` pushed to origin successfully.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #212: relation-definition ownership and protected system entry points, building on #211's normalized relation edge contract.\n\n- `CreateRelationPropertyInput` now carries independent `owner`/`ownerProcess`/`locked` per side (source and `inverse`), with `ownerProcess` required exactly when `owner: 'system'`.\n- New `SystemRelationWriteContext { ownerProcess }` gates `createRelationPropertyWithClient`, `createRelationWithClient`, `updateRelationWithClient`, `deleteRelationWithClient`. Only the property named by `relationPropertyId` authorizes an edge write; a public caller (no context) or a mismatched system context is rejected `owner_violation`.\n- The public facade (`createRelationProperty`/`createRelation`/`updateRelation`/`deleteRelation`) never passes a context, so it can never touch an `owner: 'system'` relation property.\n- Relation-property creation now applies `locked` only after both sides' schema/config is fully written, so `locked: true` never leaves an externally visible unlocked intermediate state.\n- Migrated every internal relation writer (seeds, mail ingest/draft/send/attachments/folderDiscovery/imap-gmail-graph reconcilers/personLinkingActions, `tasks/advanceTaskRecurrence`) onto the protected entry points with their registered process identity.\n- Added real-Postgres integration tests for public rejection, matching/mismatching `ownerProcess`, mixed-owner paired definitions, and atomic locked one-way/paired creation.\n\nVerified in this session: full monorepo build clean, unit tests 83/83 passing, integration tests 403/403 passing (real ephemeral Postgres).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
